{"type":"thinking","text":"Now report. Concise, with addresses, encoding, proof, survivors.\n\nLet me include the diff result quote: \"0x1E old 0 new 4\" and the fact that 175 movers survived in the stomp diff (started from walking).\n\nReport shape per skill: address, encoding, survivors each round, what the proof screenshot showed, what was written and displayed.\n\nTwo arrays:\n1. $000F-$0014 (6 slots, stride 1) enemy active flag. Encoding 1=active, 0=empty. Proof: wrote $000F=0; list_sprites dropped the Goomba's 6-tile palette-7 block.\n2. $001E-$0023 (6 slots, stride 1) enemy state. 0=walking, 4=stomped/flipped. Differential: 0→4 on stomp. Proof: wrote $001E=4; Goomba drawn upside-down.\n\nMention disassembly corroboration ($C20C spawner sets flag; $D9D4 stomp sets state 4).\n\nSummarize."}
{"type":"text","text":"Both arrays found, proven, recorded, and promoted.\n\n## Results\n\n**1. Enemy-active flag — `$000F`–`$0014`** (6 slots, stride 1, count 6; slot 0 = first Goomba)\n- Encoding: 1 byte per slot, `1` = slot active/spawned, `0` = empty/despawned.\n- Lead (disassembly): the spawner does `LDA #$01 / STA $0F,X` at CPU `$C20C`, and `$C211` reads `LDA $0F,X / BNE` to test the slot.\n- Proof: at World 1-1 with the walking Goomba on screen (`$000F` slot0 = 1, OAM slots 34–39, tiles `$FC/$FC/$70-$73`, palette 7), I paused and wrote **`$000F = 0`** (address 15), stepped 2 frames → the Goomba **disappeared**: `list_sprites` returned only the HUD coin sprite + Mario's 8 entries (9 total, no palette-7 enemy), the screenshot showed the right side empty, and RAM read `[0,0,0,0,0,0]`.\n\n**2. Enemy state — `$001E`–`$0023`** (6 slots, stride 1, count 6; slot 0 = first Goomba)\n- Encoding: 1 byte per slot; `0` = normal/walking, `4` = stomped (drawn flipped/dying); `1`/`3` are set by other behaviors; bit 7 is a dying flag.\n- Differential: `s_preStomp` (Goomba walking, `$001E` slot0 = 0) → `s_stomp` (I made Mario fall onto it; the \"100\" popup appeared) with filter `changed` returned `$001E` **0 → 4** (175 movers; the rest were position/OAM/score noise).\n- Lead (disassembly): the stomp handler at CPU `$D9D4` is `LDA #$04 / STA $1E,X`, then `INC $0484` (100-point combo) and `LDA #$FC / STA $009F` (flip/fall speed); the spawner inits it with `LDA #$00 / STA $1E,X` at `$C228`.\n- Proof: from a clean walking Goomba (`$001E` slot0 = 0, upright tiles `$FC/$FC/$70-$73`), I paused and wrote **`$001E = 4`** (address 30), stepped 2 frames → the Goomba was drawn **upside-down**: the OAM block became tile `$FC` at (208,186)/(216,186) and tile `$EF` at (208,202)/(216,202) with **flip_v** set, and the screenshot showed a flattened brown shape on the ground where the upright Goomba had been.\n\nBoth are recorded via `record_mapping` (mapping_type address, stride 1, count 6, source credited) and `promote_mappings` promoted 2 discoveries into the ROM's mapping file (now 34 addresses).\n\nOne caveat worth stating: the raw write of `$001E = 4` renders the squashed Goomba for the frame it is read, then the state-4 update recycles the byte back to 0 (there was no real collision), so that proof is the rendered pose rather than a value that persists in RAM."}
